{"notes":"SETTLED: 1. Score is shared and divided by the taller tower. Max 8 words, one word per block, in order. A full block is 1 point, one attribute right is 0.25. Targets of 9+ blocks cap the score near 0.8 or lower. 2. Confirmed words across several partners: kuru = purple ball, fuza = green star, neto = yellow ring, muva = yellow ball, loku = orange cube (generic orange), tido = blue ring, tumu = blue cube, vonu = yellow star. 3. A run of one word works only if the whole run matches the target. A wrong-shape word still earns 0.25 per block on colour alone. 4. Tentative: zeki = purple cube (one data point). 5. Cone words seem missing; colour fallback is the standard move. 6. NEW: nove is NOT red for this partner. In the last round nove nove gave purple cube, purple cube, so nove read as purple cube (or purple something) with a new partner. Meanings differ between partners, so nove is unreliable and I should not use it for red.

OPEN: 1. Still no confirmed word for red cube or any cone shape (yellow, orange, red, green, purple cone). Also missing: blue star, orange star, orange ball, purple star. 2. kano is red, shape unclear. fidi is unreliable (red cube or orange cone). mape may be green cube. vepu may be red or red ring. melu may be green ball. dobo is unknown. 3. The builder reads a one-attribute-right word as a guess, so a wrong guess costs a full block. 4. Long targets of 9+ blocks cannot be fully described, so I must choose which 8 to name.

NEXT: 1. As describer: use confirmed words (fuza, muva, kuru, neto, tido, tumu, loku, vonu). For red, test kano or vepu in a low-cost slot, one unknown word at a time, and compare the result. 2. For targets longer than 8, name the 8 blocks I have exact words for and drop trailing cone or uncertain ones. 3. As builder: zeki = purple cube, vonu = yellow star, nove may be purple cube, fidi uncertain. For unknown words, guess a block sharing colour with nearby words. 4. Match block count to word count, and do not pad."}
